\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Autoresearch integration flow diagram. The outer agent loop (dashed blue) is strictly sequential---one hypothesis, one experiment, one result per cycle. The only parallelism is internal to MIPROv2 (\texttt  {num\_threads=4} concurrent LLM evaluation calls). Tier\nobreakspace  {}1 modifies configuration only; Tier\nobreakspace  {}2 appends training examples (enforced append-only); Tier\nobreakspace  {}3 combines both. Every cycle terminates in an accept/reject decision committed to a git audit trail. Immutable safety boundaries (bottom) protect the test set (MD5 hash guard), pipeline source code, and command execution scope.}}{33}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:autoresearch_flow}{{5}{33}{Autoresearch integration flow diagram. The outer agent loop (dashed blue) is strictly sequential---one hypothesis, one experiment, one result per cycle. The only parallelism is internal to MIPROv2 (\texttt {num\_threads=4} concurrent LLM evaluation calls). Tier~1 modifies configuration only; Tier~2 appends training examples (enforced append-only); Tier~3 combines both. Every cycle terminates in an accept/reject decision committed to a git audit trail. Immutable safety boundaries (bottom) protect the test set (MD5 hash guard), pipeline source code, and command execution scope}{figure.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Product maturity model showing the progression from Tier\nobreakspace  {}1 (safe configuration tuning) through Tier\nobreakspace  {}2 (human-gated data augmentation) to Tier\nobreakspace  {}3 (fully autonomous combined optimization). Each tier has a defined risk profile, supervision requirement, graduation gate, and client value proposition. The compounding effect (right) illustrates why Tier\nobreakspace  {}3 is more than the sum of Tiers\nobreakspace  {}1 and\nobreakspace  {}2: richer data changes which configs are optimal, and better configs reveal which data gaps matter most.}}{34}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:maturity}{{6}{34}{Product maturity model showing the progression from Tier~1 (safe configuration tuning) through Tier~2 (human-gated data augmentation) to Tier~3 (fully autonomous combined optimization). Each tier has a defined risk profile, supervision requirement, graduation gate, and client value proposition. The compounding effect (right) illustrates why Tier~3 is more than the sum of Tiers~1 and~2: richer data changes which configs are optimal, and better configs reveal which data gaps matter most}{figure.6}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces MIPROv2 optimization trajectory (Claude Sonnet\nobreakspace  {}4.6 compile, Claude Opus\nobreakspace  {}4.6 inference, \texttt  {heavy} setting): composite metric scores across 66 Bayesian optimization trials (left) and score distribution (right). The zero-shot baseline (83.2\%) is shown in red; the best trial reached 87.29\% composite. A prior compilation with Nemotron\nobreakspace  {}120B / Qwen3.5-27B peaked at 87.04\% after 33 trials against a much lower baseline (68--73\%), confirming that inference model capability is the dominant performance factor.}}{35}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:miprov2}{{7}{35}{MIPROv2 optimization trajectory (Claude Sonnet~4.6 compile, Claude Opus~4.6 inference, \texttt {heavy} setting): composite metric scores across 66 Bayesian optimization trials (left) and score distribution (right). The zero-shot baseline (83.2\%) is shown in red; the best trial reached 87.29\% composite. A prior compilation with Nemotron~120B / Qwen3.5-27B peaked at 87.04\% after 33 trials against a much lower baseline (68--73\%), confirming that inference model capability is the dominant performance factor}{figure.7}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Held-out test set results (17 examples). Left: confusion matrix showing zero false positives and two false negatives in \texttt  {affiliation\_bias} (compliance gatekeeping pattern). Right: per-category precision and recall---perfect scores across all categories except \texttt  {affiliation\_bias} recall (60\%).}}{35}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:confusion}{{8}{35}{Held-out test set results (17 examples). Left: confusion matrix showing zero false positives and two false negatives in \texttt {affiliation\_bias} (compliance gatekeeping pattern). Right: per-category precision and recall---perfect scores across all categories except \texttt {affiliation\_bias} recall (60\%)}{figure.8}{}}
